# Line-ending policy.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Twenty test files read this repository's own source with
# readFileSync and assert on its text. The egress guard's transport test, for one,
# slices guard.ts on a literal written with an LF newline. With core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout smudges an LF blob to CRLF in the working tree, so the identical
# commit passes on Linux CI and fails on Windows. Pinning the module sources to LF
# makes the working tree match the blob on every platform, which is what those
# assertions already assume.
#
# DELIBERATELY NARROW. Only the two module classes the test suite parses. Markdown,
# JSON evidence, HTML fixtures and .js keep the existing convention, so this
# normalises seven enumerated files and nothing else. Recorded evidence is
# unaffected: the one harness that digests its own source (E2's harnessSha256LF)
# normalises to LF before hashing.
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.cts  text eol=lf
*.mts  text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
